      },
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "school-body",
          "title": "The Old School",
          "text": "The old school building became a meeting place after classes ended. People used the hall for choir rehearsals, history evenings, and winter gatherings.\n\nIn winter, the caretaker lit the tiled stove before dawn. Matti wrote that the windows stayed frosted until the first song began, and that the harbour families brought coffee in enamel pots wrapped with wool scarves.",
          "privacy": {
            "privacyScope": "public",
            "consentStatus": "not_required",
            "livingPersonStatus": "not_applicable",
